Subject: [PATCH] power: sequencing: pwrseq-pcie-m2: Add QCC2072 BT PCI device ID

Upstream: qcom-next bc2b6da4d0b5 ("FROMGIT: power: sequencing: pwrseq-pcie-m2: Add QCC2072
BT PCI device ID"); v2 patch 3/6 of "Bluetooth: qca: enable QCC2072". Dropped from
pwrseq/for-next until the qcom,qcc2072-bt binding is documented.
With it, the M.2 E-key connector creates the Bluetooth serdev for PCI 17cb:1112.
---
--- a/drivers/power/sequencing/pwrseq-pcie-m2.c
+++ b/drivers/power/sequencing/pwrseq-pcie-m2.c
@@ -202,6 +202,8 @@
 	/* Qualcomm's default subsystem ID, used by the Surface Laptop 8 */
 	{ PCI_DEVICE_SUB(PCI_VENDOR_ID_QCOM, 0x1107, PCI_VENDOR_ID_QCOM, 0x1107),
 	  .driver_data = (kernel_ulong_t)"qcom,wcn7850-bt" },
+	{ PCI_DEVICE(PCI_VENDOR_ID_QCOM, 0x1112),
+	  .driver_data = (kernel_ulong_t)"qcom,qcc2072-bt" },
 	{ } /* Sentinel */
 };
 
